{"key":"moonbitlang/x/rational.Rational.is_integer:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/x/rational","name":"is_integer","parent":"moonbitlang/x/rational.Rational","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[T : Integral] Rational::is_integer(Self[T]) -> Bool","doc":"Checks whether the rational number represents an integer value.\n\n Parameters:\n\n * `self` : The rational number to check.\n\n Returns `true` if the rational number is an integer (has a denominator of 1),\n `false` otherwise.\n\n Examples:\n\n ```moonbit check\n test {\n   let half = @rational.new(1L, 2L).unwrap()\n   inspect(half.is_integer(), content=\"false\")\n   let whole = @rational.new(5L, 1L).unwrap()\n   inspect(whole.is_integer(), content=\"true\")\n   let zero = @rational.new(0L, 1L).unwrap()\n   inspect(zero.is_integer(), content=\"true\")\n }\n ```","attrs":[["as_free_fn",null,false]]}
