{"key":"moonbitlang/x/rational.Rational32","pkg":"moonbitlang/x/rational","name":"Rational32","parent":"moonbitlang/x/rational","kind":["type_alias","moonbitlang/x/rational.Rational"],"sig_":"pub type Rational32 = Rational[Int]","doc":"Rational number type.\n\n Invariants:\n - The denominator is always positive.\n - The numerator and denominator are always coprime.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/x/path/win32.Path.normalize:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/x/path/win32","name":"normalize","parent":"moonbitlang/x/path/win32.Path","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn Path::normalize(Self) -> Self","doc":"1. resolve `.` by directly removing it\n 2. resolve `..` by removing the preceding path component if exists, otherwise keep it.\n 3. remove redundant backslashes \n 4. preserve trailing slash or backslash\n \n edge cases:\n   1. when path is empty, return empty string\n \n ```moonbit check\n test {\n   let path : Path = \"C:\\\\usr\\\\\\\\local\\\\..\\\\bin\\\\\"\n   inspect(path.normalize(), content=\"C:\\\\usr\\\\bin\")\n }\n ```","attrs":[]}
