{"key":"moonbitlang/x/decimal.Decimal.from_string:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/x/decimal","name":"from_string","parent":"moonbitlang/x/decimal.Decimal","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn Decimal::from_string(String) -> Self?","doc":"Creates a decimal from a string representation.\n\n Parameters:\n * `s` : String representation of the decimal (e.g., \"123.45\", \"-0.001\")\n\n Returns `Some(decimal)` if parsing succeeds, `None` otherwise.\n\n Example:\n ```moonbit check\n test {\n   let d = match @decimal.Decimal::from_string(\"123.45\") {\n     Some(d) => d\n     None => fail(\"Invalid decimal string\")\n   }\n   inspect(d.to_string(), content=\"123.45\")\n }\n ```","attrs":[]}
