{"key":"moonbitlang/x/rational.Rational.abs:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/x/rational","name":"abs","parent":"moonbitlang/x/rational.Rational","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[T : Integral] Rational::abs(Self[T]) -> Self[T]","doc":"Returns the absolute value of a rational number.\n\n Parameters:\n\n * `self` : The rational number to get the absolute value of.\n\n Returns a new rational number representing the absolute value of the input.\n\n Example:\n\n ```moonbit check\n test {\n   let positive = @rational.new(3L, 4L).unwrap()\n   let negative = @rational.new(-3L, 4L).unwrap()\n   inspect(positive.abs(), content=\"3/4\")\n   inspect(negative.abs(), content=\"3/4\")\n }\n ```","attrs":[["as_free_fn",null,false]]}
