{"key":"moonbitlang/x/rational.Rational.to_double:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/x/rational","name":"to_double","parent":"moonbitlang/x/rational.Rational","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn Rational::to_double(Self[Int64]) -> Double","doc":"Converts the rational number to its approximate double-precision\n floating-point representation.\n\n Parameters:\n\n * `self` : The rational number to convert.\n\n Returns the double-precision floating-point approximation of the rational\n number.\n\n Example:\n\n ```moonbit check\n test {\n   let rational = @rational.new(1L, 2L).unwrap()\n   inspect(rational.to_double(), content=\"0.5\")\n   let negative = @rational.new(-3L, 4L).unwrap()\n   inspect(negative.to_double(), content=\"-0.75\")\n }\n ```","attrs":[]}
